\title{vosa: Variance-Optimized Saliences Analysis for multiblock data}
\description{
The package computes, for a list of scalar product matrices \eqn{W_k = X_k X_k'} (one per block, scaled to unit trace), components described by their saliences \eqn{a_k(u) = u'W_ku}, the share of the inertia of block \eqn{k} reproduced by the component \eqn{u}.

The level \eqn{\bar a(u)} and the contrast \eqn{V(u)} of a component are the mean and the variance of its saliences. The family \eqn{g_\alpha = (1-\alpha)\bar a^2 + \alpha V} contains CPCA (\code{\link{cpca}}, \eqn{\alpha = 0}), INDORT (\code{\link{indort}}, \eqn{\alpha = 1/2}) and VOSA (\code{\link{vosa}}, \eqn{\alpha = 1}); \code{\link{spa}} solves any \eqn{\alpha} and \code{\link{chemin_spa}} the whole path. \code{\link{statis}} is provided for comparison.

\code{\link{factorisation_canonique}} writes any fit in the canonical factorization \eqn{X_k = U D_k V_k' + E_k}, and \code{\link{plot_U}}, \code{\link{plot_D}} and \code{\link{plot_V}} draw its components, diagonal terms and loadings; \code{\link{plafonds}}, \code{\link{diagnostic_blocs}}, \code{\link{heterogeneite}} and \code{\link{borne_relative}} give the diagnostics of the article; \code{\link{simuler_blocs}} generates the simulated data.

The script that reproduces the results of the article is installed with the package: \code{system.file("scripts", "reproduire_article.R", package = "vosa")}.
}
\references{
Ballah Houssein, S., Galharret, J.-M. and Hanafi, M. (2026). VOSA: variance-optimized saliences analysis. Manuscript.

Bougeard, S., Peltier, C., Jaillais, B., Boulet, J.-C. and Hanafi, M. (2024). Benchmarking multiblock methods with canonical factorization. Chemometrics and Intelligent Laboratory Systems, 254, 105240.
